139.steps:
1. Load the firmware on the SonicWALL and boot with default settings.
2. Configure interface X2 LAN, connect to Router. Configure secondary WAN interface.
3. Configure OSPF on the Router (don't use 10.0.0.1 router-ID): Router>router ospf Router>network area 0 , originate default-information always on the Router.
4. On the Network>Routing page of SonicWALL, select Advanced Routing mode. Configure OSPF for X2 interface: OSPFv2: Enabled Area: 0 Area Type: Normal Router-ID: 10.0.0.1 ;
5. Change the metric of default route received from advanced routing protocols from 110 to 10;
6. Click on the Neighbor Status LED to see full adjacency with the Router. Check FW's routing table.

141.steps:
step 1, Configure a new interface X3 with zone LAN and IP 28.1.1.2 in IPv4 interface page, interface X3's interface speed is 1Gbps;
step 2, Navigate to Network->Routing, enable OSPF on X3;
step 3, X3 OSPF interface cost is in auto mode;
step 4, Change Auto-Cost Reference BW to 40000 Mb/sec;
step 5, Connect a router to interface X3, and config OSPF on router;
step 6, Check X3 Interface Cost, it should be 40;
step 7, Repeat step 1 to step 6 on a 10Gbps interface;
step 8, Repeat step 1 to step 6 on a 10Mbps interface;
step 9, Repeat step 1 to step 6 on a 100Mbps interface;
step 10, Repeat step 1 to step 9 on a vlan sub-interface.�

141.result:
in step 6, the interface cost displayed on OSPF edit page should be 40.
CLI output will show details about DUT router-lsa, the metric = Auto-Cost Reference BW/Real Bandwidth, in this case, it should be 40;
in step 7, when interface real bandwidth is 10Gbps, then the interface cost calculated by the default reference bandwidth should be 4;
in step 8, when interface real bandwidth is 10Mbps, then the interface cost calculated by the default reference bandwidth should be 4000;
in step 9, when interface real bandwidth is 100Mbps, then the interface cost calculated by the default reference bandwidth should be 400;
in step 10, the vlan sub interface should inherit its parent interface' link speed to caculate the ospf cost, so the test results should be same as above.�

156.steps:
1. Add site to site VPN policy on local and remote FW, and use an AO Group as the local and remote network;
2. Enable OSPF/RIP on DUT, redistribute the remote VPN network;
3. Use command "show ip route ospf" on router;
4. Disable site to site VPN policy, check router "show ip route ospf".

156.result:
in step 1, make sure the VPN policy is established;
in step 2, make sure OSPF neighbor established;
in step 3, make sure router learned the remote VPN network from DUT;
in step 4, make sure when the VPN is down, the remote VPN network routes disappeared on router.

140.steps:
step 1, Configure a new interface X3 with zone LAN and IP 28.1.1.2 in IPv4 interface page, interface X3's interface speed is 1Gbps;
step 2, Navigate to Network->Routing, enable OSPF on X3;
step 3, X3 OSPF interface cost is in auto mode;
step 4, Auto-Cost Reference BW default value is 100 Mb/sec;
step 5, Connect a router to interface X3, and config OSPF on router;
step 6, Check X3 Interface Cost, it should be 1;
step 7, Repeat step 1 to step 6 on a 10Gbps interface;
step 8, Repeat step 1 to step 6 on a 10Mbps interface;
step 9, Repeat step 1 to step 6 on a 100Mbps interface;
step 10, Repeat step 1-9 on vlan sub-interface.�

140.result:
in step 6, the interface cost displayed on OSPF edit page should be 1.
CLI output will show details about DUT router-lsa, the metric = Auto-Cost Reference BW/Real Bandwidth, in this case, it should be 1;
in step 7, when interface real bandwidth is 10Gbps, then the interface cost calculated by the default reference bandwidth should be 1;
in step 8, when interface real bandwidth is 10Mbps, then the interface cost calculated by the default reference bandwidth should be 10;
in step 9, when interface real bandwidth is 100Mbps, then the interface cost calculated by the default reference bandwidth should be 1;
in step 10, vlan sub-interface should inherit its parent interface' link speed to caculate the ospf cost, the test results should be same as above.
